<p class="sst-lead">The SRQD sends every shape to a pair \(\big([\widetilde{X}_k],\,P_k\big)\). The undulation factor
lives on a <strong>Grassmannian</strong> via the canonical projection.</p>

<p>\[ \pi: X \mapsto [X],\qquad \pi(\mathbb{R}^{n\times2}_*) = \mathrm{Gr}(2,n). \]</p>

<div class="sst-frag">
  <p>It is surjective, <strong>scale-invariant</strong> \(\pi(XM)=\pi(X)\) for \(M\in GL(2)\), and idempotent.
  The whole fiber &mdash; the \(GL(2)\) orbit of linear rescalings &mdash; collapses to one point of undulation.</p>
  <p class="sst-note">That's why \([\widetilde{X}]\) is a clean invariant of shape: the scale we factored into \(P\)
  is exactly the fiber direction \(\pi\) quotients away.</p>
</div>
